;; MUST-FAIL FIXTURE (an internal review, a finding) — SALE half. The deploy footer's upgrade branch must REFUSE a
;; chain that never received the fresh deploy.
;;
;; 🔴 THE DEFECT THIS PINS. Sending the artifact as `upgrade:true` to a chain with no prior module
;; fresh-installs it CLEANLY — Pact does not evaluate GOVERNANCE when the module is absent, so
;; nothing authorises anything and the upgrade branch creates NO TABLES. With the freeze artifact
;; that lands a permanently frozen module with no tables: every stateful function aborts, GOVERNANCE
;; refuses every repair forever, and our own post-freeze verification calls that chain correct
;; (identical hash, identical stored code). One operator keystroke, one unrecoverable chain, across a
;; 20-chain train where a missed chain is exactly the precondition.
;;
;; 🔴 WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A FROZEN FIXTURE. run-tests.sh's gen_frozen DELETES the real
;; footer from /^(if (read-msg 'upgrade)$/ to EOF and substitutes a two-line stub, and the devnet
;; freeze drill synthesises its own. So NO existing test has ever exercised the real footer. This
;; fixture loads the REAL module file, so the footer under test is the one that ships. The freeze
;; is not needed to demonstrate it — the refusal fires on any tableless upgrade — and leaving the
;; freeze out is what lets this pin the shipping bytes instead of a generated copy.
;;
;; Falsifying: revert the footer's upgrade branch to the bare string and this fixture STOPS failing.
